WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:18.073
Unit forty-nine: Leadership and Ethics. In this unit, you will evaluate what makes leadership ethical.

4
00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:20.433
ethical leadership.

5
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:27.126
ethical leadership means leading by doing what is right, not only what is profitable or popular.

6
00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.482
Ethical leadership means admitting mistakes publicly.

7
00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:34.578
Your turn. Say: ethical leadership.

8
00:00:37.278 --> 00:00:38.511
ethical leadership.

9
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:41.040
authentic leadership.

10
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.874
authentic leadership means leadership based on honesty about one's own values and limits.

11
00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:50.985
Authentic leadership builds trust because people see the real person.

12
00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:55.429
Your turn. Say: authentic leadership.

13
00:00:58.129 --> 00:00:59.513
authentic leadership.

14
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:01.854
toxic leadership.

15
00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:08.049
toxic leadership means leadership that harms people through fear, bullying or selfishness.

16
00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:11.184
Toxic leadership drove half the team to resign.

17
00:01:11.884 --> 00:01:15.082
Your turn. Say: toxic leadership.

18
00:01:17.782 --> 00:01:19.108
toxic leadership.

19
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:21.605
stewardship leadership.

20
00:01:22.305 --> 00:01:28.821
stewardship leadership means leading as a caretaker of resources for future generations.

21
00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:33.408
Stewardship leadership protects the forest the company depends on.

22
00:01:34.108 --> 00:01:37.770
Your turn. Say: stewardship leadership.

23
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.889
stewardship leadership.

24
00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:44.755
transformational leadership.

25
00:01:45.455 --> 00:01:51.762
transformational leadership means leadership that inspires people to change and exceed expectations.

26
00:01:52.062 --> 00:01:55.954
Transformational leadership turned a failing school into a model.

27
00:01:56.654 --> 00:01:59.945
Your turn. Say: transformational leadership.

28
00:02:02.645 --> 00:02:04.528
transformational leadership.

29
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:06.936
leadership legacy.

30
00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:11.388
leadership legacy means what a leader leaves behind for others.

31
00:02:11.688 --> 00:02:15.847
Her leadership legacy is a generation of confident young women.

32
00:02:16.547 --> 00:02:19.734
Your turn. Say: leadership legacy.

33
00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.004
leadership legacy.

34
00:02:25.017 --> 00:02:26.726
integrity in office.

35
00:02:27.426 --> 00:02:33.350
integrity in office means honest and principled behaviour while holding power.

36
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:38.563
Integrity in office means refusing gifts that create obligations.

37
00:02:39.263 --> 00:02:43.088
Your turn. Say: integrity in office.

38
00:02:45.788 --> 00:02:47.463
integrity in office.

39
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.753
moral compass.

40
00:02:50.453 --> 00:02:55.320
moral compass means a person's inner sense of right and wrong that guides decisions.

41
00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.572
A leader without a moral compass will follow the money.

42
00:02:59.272 --> 00:03:02.772
Your turn. Say: moral compass.

43
00:03:05.472 --> 00:03:06.716
moral compass.

44
00:03:07.717 --> 00:03:09.948
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:10.248 --> 00:03:14.558
Ms. Sarah, can a leader be successful and ethical at the same time?

46
00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:19.152
Of course. But power can go to anyone's head.

47
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.007
So leaders need a strong moral compass.

48
00:03:24.317 --> 00:03:29.012
Exactly. Otherwise they sail wherever the wind of profit blows.

49
00:03:30.317 --> 00:03:33.837
Toxic leaders seem to rule with an iron fist.

50
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.742
They do, and they leave scorched earth behind them.

51
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.189
What about transformational leaders?

52
00:03:42.483 --> 00:03:47.423
They plant trees whose shade they will never sit in. That is a true leadership legacy.

53
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:53.259
Grammar focus: Idioms and figurative language (advanced).

54
00:03:53.559 --> 00:03:56.905
Figurative language makes leadership ideas memorable.

55
00:03:57.205 --> 00:04:01.773
Power can go to anyone's head. Toxic leaders rule with an iron fist.

56
00:04:02.073 --> 00:04:05.466
Great leaders plant trees whose shade they will never sit in.

57
00:04:05.766 --> 00:04:12.630
Extend a metaphor carefully: a moral compass can guide a ship, but don't mix it with a train in the same sentence.

58
00:04:13.617 --> 00:04:16.942
Now read and listen. The Leader's Inner Compass.

59
00:04:17.242 --> 00:04:22.388
Leadership has been studied for centuries, yet its ethical dimension is often overlooked.

60
00:04:23.683 --> 00:04:29.526
Ethical leadership requires more than achieving results; it asks how those results are achieved.

61
00:04:30.817 --> 00:04:38.807
Authentic leadership emphasises self-awareness and honesty, allowing followers to trust the person behind the title.

62
00:04:40.117 --> 00:04:45.808
Transformational leadership inspires people to pursue shared goals beyond their own interests.

63
00:04:47.117 --> 00:04:55.211
Toxic leadership, by contrast, relies on fear and leaves organisations damaged long after the leader departs.

64
00:04:56.517 --> 00:05:01.639
Stewardship leadership sees power as something held in trust for future generations.

65
00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:07.515
Integrity in office is tested most severely when no one is watching.

66
00:05:08.817 --> 00:05:15.182
Ultimately, a leader's legacy depends less on titles than on the moral compass that guided every decision.

67
00:05:16.483 --> 00:05:18.985
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:22.956
A person's inner sense of right and wrong is a blank.

69
00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:28.372
A, moral compass. B, leadership legacy. C, toxic leadership.

70
00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:35.184
The answer is A: moral compass.

71
00:05:36.683 --> 00:05:39.356
'Power went to his head' means he became blank.

72
00:05:39.656 --> 00:05:43.159
A, arrogant. B, intelligent. C, tired.

73
00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.544
The answer is A: arrogant.

74
00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.723
'Rule with an iron fist' means rule blank.

75
00:05:54.023 --> 00:05:57.688
A, harshly. B, fairly. C, weakly.

76
00:06:01.683 --> 00:06:03.427
The answer is A: harshly.

77
00:06:04.917 --> 00:06:09.517
Leadership that inspires people to exceed expectations is blank.

78
00:06:09.817 --> 00:06:15.502
A, transformational leadership. B, toxic leadership. C, stewardship leadership.

79
00:06:19.517 --> 00:06:22.654
The answer is A: transformational leadership.

80
00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:29.040
According to the text, when is integrity in office tested most severely?

81
00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:34.933
A, when no one is watching. B, during elections. C, in public speeches.

82
00:06:38.917 --> 00:06:41.729
The answer is A: when no one is watching.

83
00:06:43.217 --> 00:06:48.609
Now it's your turn. Part one: Describe a leader you admire and explain what makes them ethical.

84
00:06:53.909 --> 00:06:58.323
Part two: Use one idiom and one extended metaphor.

85
00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:17.692
My grandfather led our village association. Power never went to his head. He planted trees whose shade he would never sit in: a school, a well and a savings group that still helps families today.

86
00:07:17.992 --> 00:07:20.097
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:21.083 --> 00:07:26.580
Great work today! You learned eight new words and idioms and figurative language (advanced).

88
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.309
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

89
00:07:31.609 --> 00:07:34.435
See you in Unit fifty. Goodbye!

90
00:07:34.735 --> 00:07:37.306
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

